From 25146ea50b064ea49d55c8ebb3a17c0129bf6492 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: add Samsung Galaxy S10 / S10+
 (beyond1lte, beyond2lte)

The full board DT of the Galaxy S10 / S10+ (exynos9820.dtsi, the common
board part with its audio and camera includes, and the two board
files), with the one dt-bindings header it needs. The kernel package
ships the DTB and it is the only full DT of the device: the bootloader
(U-Boot) only carries a base DT for its own use and applies its
boot-time fixups (memory, /chosen, serial-number) to the DTB it is
given.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
